                <pb facs="0581" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/833: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Collier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-31T17:00:00-04:42"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:50
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your 12, January 30, 4 p.m. I have notified the Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    of Peru’s acceptance. He told me confidentially that <pb facs="0582" n="462"
                        xml:id="pg462"/> Chile will within 2 days announce the appointment of Carlos
                    Aldunate Solar, chief of the Conservative Party, and of Luís Izquierdo, the
                    Chilean Minister to Argentina, as delegates to the meeting in Washington. They
                    prefer that the date be fixed by President Harding, and suggest the last half of
                    March. The President’s reply to the telegram from the President of Bolivia has
                    been published here, and commented on editorially as indicating that the only
                    questions to be arbitrated are those which have grown out of the Treaty of
                    Ancón, to which Bolivia was not a party.</p>
                <p>Tomorrow the Minister of Foreign Affairs will leave for Tacna to consider
                    questions of administration and to investigate the Peruvian charge of unjust
                    expulsions. He will be away for 10 days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
